WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:16.488
"Danger for all Gliss cried, echoing the crow's warning.

2
00:00:16.508 --> 00:00:17.868
"What does that mean?"

3
00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:20.889
"Hush," Professor Liblow said again.

4
00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:22.689
"Let it finish its message."

5
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.630
Echo crows didn't talk on their own.

6
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.971
They could only repeat what a person told them.

7
00:00:28.931 --> 00:00:30.131
The crow flapped its wings.

8
00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:32.212
"Urgent danger," it said again.

9
00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:35.089
"Reds are disappearing all over Magica.

10
00:00:35.349 --> 00:00:37.910
Nobody knows where they went or what has become of them.

11
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.671
All Reds, please take precautions.

12
00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:42.152
Urgent, urgent."

13
00:00:43.132 --> 00:00:44.753
The echo crow clacked its beak.

14
00:00:45.493 --> 00:00:46.654
Then it flew out of the room.

15
00:00:47.654 --> 00:00:49.115
Everyone started talking at once.

16
00:00:50.955 --> 00:00:52.296
Well, almost everyone.

17
00:00:52.756 --> 00:00:53.917
Zann didn't say a word.

18
00:00:54.237 --> 00:00:56.618
The crow's message had made him think about his parents.

19
00:00:57.358 --> 00:01:00.139
Nobody knew where they were either, or what had become of them.

20
00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:01.660
But that was different.

21
00:01:01.996 --> 00:01:03.397
For one thing, they weren't Reds.

22
00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:07.119
For another, they had disappeared four long years ago.

23
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:09.420
Perda poked him.

24
00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.041
"Did you hear that?"

25
00:01:11.461 --> 00:01:11.821
she said.

26
00:01:11.841 --> 00:01:13.542
"What do you think it means?"

27
00:01:13.562 --> 00:01:17.825
"Silence!" Professor Liblow cried.

28
00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:21.367
His voice boomed, with the help of a Swelling spell.

29
00:01:22.107 --> 00:01:23.588
The class quieted down at once.

30
00:01:24.368 --> 00:01:25.409
Gliss raised her hand.

31
00:01:25.429 --> 00:01:28.851
"I need to go home," she said, her voice cracking.

32
00:01:29.491 --> 00:01:31.032
"Both of my parents are Reds.

33
00:01:31.796 --> 00:01:33.637
I should tell them about this warning!"

34
00:01:33.657 --> 00:01:36.239
"Me too," Zann said.

35
00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:38.840
"My grandfather, Boz, is a Red."

36
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.661
"What's the big deal?"

37
00:01:41.001 --> 00:01:44.103
Jev's voice was loud enough for Zann to hear, but not the teacher.

38
00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:48.365
"All those snooty Reds are probably sneaking off somewhere together.

39
00:01:49.085 --> 00:01:53.128
Maybe they're trying to come up with even more ways to act superior to the rest of us."

40
00:01:54.128 --> 00:01:55.269
"Be quiet, Jev."

41
00:01:55.589 --> 00:01:56.610
Perda glared at him.

42
00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.370
"You're just jealous."

43
00:01:59.571 --> 00:02:01.752
Gliss hadn't heard Jev.

44
00:02:01.772 --> 00:02:02.312
She stood up.

45
00:02:02.332 --> 00:02:04.773
"I just remembered something," she said.

46
00:02:04.793 --> 00:02:08.095
"Last night I overheard my parents whispering."

47
00:02:08.835 --> 00:02:10.436
"You overheard them?"

48
00:02:10.856 --> 00:02:13.097
Professor Liblow gave her a suspicious look.

49
00:02:13.577 --> 00:02:16.018
"How?" Gliss blushed.

50
00:02:16.038 --> 00:02:17.518
"Okay, I admit it.

51
00:02:17.879 --> 00:02:19.119
I used a spy fly.

52
00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:22.240
I know we're not supposed to use them to spy on people.

53
00:02:22.881 --> 00:02:25.882
But my parents wouldn't tell me why they look so worried lately.

54
00:02:26.642 --> 00:02:28.483
I had to find out what's going on!"

55
00:02:28.503 --> 00:02:31.768
"Wow," thought Zann.

56
00:02:31.788 --> 00:02:35.009
If Gliss had used a spy fly, she must have been very concerned.

57
00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:36.969
"So what did you hear?"

58
00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:37.830
he asked.

59
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.811
"It was about my uncle," Gliss said.

60
00:02:40.831 --> 00:02:42.331
"He lives in New Mist."

61
00:02:43.131 --> 00:02:44.932
"You mean the town near Mount Mystery?"

62
00:02:45.392 --> 00:02:45.872
Zann said.

63
00:02:45.892 --> 00:02:50.413
"My parents haven't heard from Uncle Gar in three days," Gliss said.

64
00:02:50.433 --> 00:02:52.174
"He's a Red too."

65
00:02:52.194 --> 00:02:53.934
"Oh dear."

66
00:02:54.594 --> 00:02:56.135
Professor Liblow shook his head.

67
00:02:56.155 --> 00:02:58.555
"This sounds rather serious.

68
00:02:59.256 --> 00:03:02.692
Perhaps you'd better go home It's almost time to go anyway.

69
00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:03.933
Class dismissed."

70
00:03:04.793 --> 00:03:08.474
The students started gathering their things and chattering about what had just happened.

71
00:03:08.994 --> 00:03:11.755
Zann grabbed his bag and hurried out of the room with Perda.

72
00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:17.677
"I should find out what Boz knows about this," Zann said.

73
00:03:18.377 --> 00:03:20.557
"He's a retired Magic Master, remember?

74
00:03:21.478 --> 00:03:24.318
Maybe some of his friends in the capital know what's going on."

75
00:03:25.559 --> 00:03:26.459
Perda gave him a look.

76
00:03:26.479 --> 00:03:29.400
"You sound almost excited," she said.

77
00:03:30.048 --> 00:03:30.948
"Aren't you scared?

78
00:03:31.229 --> 00:03:32.649
You and Boz are both Reds."

79
00:03:33.369 --> 00:03:36.871
Before Zann could respond, Jev came into the hall with some friends.

80
00:03:37.991 --> 00:03:40.512
"Rushing home to hide under your bed, Red?"

81
00:03:40.892 --> 00:03:41.553
Jev jeered.

82
00:03:42.353 --> 00:03:43.313
Zann didn't answer.

83
00:03:44.394 --> 00:03:49.676
Jev had never forgiven him for an incident on Zann's first day at the Swamp Bottom School almost

84
00:03:49.816 --> 00:03:50.976
four years earlier.

85
00:03:51.677 --> 00:03:54.838
But even if that had never happened, they still wouldn't be friends.

86
00:03:55.618 --> 00:03:57.339
Jev seemed to hate all Reds.

87
00:03:58.079 --> 00:03:59.360
Well, not all Reds.

88
00:04:00.032 --> 00:04:06.094
Just then Gliss hurried out of the classroom, and Jev's voice instantly changed from sneering to sympathetic.

89
00:04:06.114 --> 00:04:07.754
"Hey, Gliss.

90
00:04:08.074 --> 00:04:09.415
Sorry your uncle is missing.

91
00:04:09.735 --> 00:04:10.855
Want me to walk you home?"

92
00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:12.636
"Thanks, that's sweet.

93
00:04:12.916 --> 00:04:14.716
But I'm in too much of a hurry to walk."

94
00:04:15.416 --> 00:04:18.157
Gliss rubbed her hands together and muttered the word "zap."

95
00:04:18.897 --> 00:04:20.638
A second later she disappeared.

96
00:04:21.278 --> 00:04:23.739
Jev frowned and then zapped himself away too.

97
00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:26.299
Zann was glad to see him go.

98
00:04:26.319 --> 00:04:28.540
"Come on," he told Perda.

99
00:04:29.284 --> 00:04:32.606
"I'll walk you home in case you're afraid of disappearing without a trace."

100
00:04:32.626 --> 00:04:36.988
"I'm not the one who should be afraid," she retorted.

101
00:04:37.008 --> 00:04:39.870
"The crow said the warning was only for Reds."

102
00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.211
"Okay," Zann said.

103
00:04:42.231 --> 00:04:44.032
"Then you can walk me home."

104
00:04:44.872 --> 00:04:45.453
She smiled.

105
00:04:45.473 --> 00:04:46.393
"It's a deal.

106
00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:47.214
Let's go."

107
00:04:48.034 --> 00:04:48.935
They headed for home.

108
00:04:51.376 --> 00:04:56.799
It was a bright, clear day with a light breeze that blew Perda's soft, caramel-colored hair around her

109
00:04:56.859 --> 00:05:00.881
face. Was it magic, or did she seem to get prettier every day?

110
00:05:01.741 --> 00:05:03.161
Zann tried not to notice that.

111
00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:08.523
It made him feel confused and nervous— a lot more nervous than he'd felt on hearing the echo

112
00:05:08.563 --> 00:05:09.303
crow's message.

113
00:05:10.003 --> 00:05:12.244
When they reached Perda's house, she sighed.

114
00:05:12.264 --> 00:05:15.505
"Looks like Mom's been redecorating again."

115
00:05:16.805 --> 00:05:20.486
The house had been square and blue that morning when the kids left for school.

116
00:05:21.246 --> 00:05:22.967
Now it was a multicolored blob.

117
00:05:22.987 --> 00:05:26.428
"Hey, she lives in Swamp Bottom, remember?"

118
00:05:26.808 --> 00:05:27.428
Zann joked.

119
00:05:28.076 --> 00:05:30.297
"She has to do something to lessen the boredom."

120
00:05:31.118 --> 00:05:32.158
Perda rolled her eyes.

121
00:05:32.178 --> 00:05:34.500
"See you tomorrow," she said.

122
00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.062
"Bye." Zann headed next door.

123
00:05:38.942 --> 00:05:43.625
His grandfather wasn't very interested in redecorating, so their house looked the same as always.

124
00:05:46.807 --> 00:05:50.308
In other words, it was just as boring as everything else in Swamp Bottom.

125
00:05:50.989 --> 00:05:54.091
For a second Zann wondered how his mother might redecorate the place.

126
00:05:54.871 --> 00:05:56.332
She'd always been good at that sort of thing.

127
00:05:57.332 --> 00:06:02.958
She'd loved to surprise him by turning his bedroom into a spooky cave or a mysterious jungle He

128
00:06:02.998 --> 00:06:06.242
snapped out of those thoughts when he heard a rustling sound directly overhead.

129
00:06:07.063 --> 00:06:12.469
Glancing up, he barely had time to take in a dragon's snarling face hissing down at him.

130
00:06:12.489 --> 00:06:13.890
Zann jumped back just in time.

131
00:06:14.651 --> 00:06:19.136
A bolt of flame sizzled down, incinerating the ground where he'd just stood.
